# Custom IPv4 rules for Issabel.
#
# Copy this file to a name ending in .rules (for example 20-custom.rules),
# remove the leading '#' from the lines you need and run:
#
#   issabel-firewall apply
#
# The file must be root:root and must not be writable by group or others.
# Use the Issabel chains: ISSABEL_HIGH, ISSABEL_BLOCK, ISSABEL_INPUT,
# ISSABEL_FORWARD, ISSABEL_OUTPUT.

*filter
# -A ISSABEL_INPUT -p tcp --dport 8443 -j ACCEPT
# -A ISSABEL_HIGH  -s 203.0.113.0/24 -p tcp --dport 1194 -j ACCEPT
COMMIT
